  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5567",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological activity of BeWo cells through a series of molecular interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, P2X purinoceptor 1, or Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, all of which are subsequently targeted by palmarumycin CP18. This chain of targets ultimately leads to the interaction with BeWo cells, indicating a potential mechanism by which Mollicellin N influences BeWo cell behavior. The overlapping role of palmarumycin CP18 as a common mediator across different targets highlights a possible central function in the biological response to Mollicellin N. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of palmarumycin CP18 in mediating the effects of Mollicellin N on BeWo cells, suggesting a complex yet interconnected network of molecular interactions.",
